TensorFold
----------
The engine patches apply to TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. scripts/build-engine.sh clones TensorFold at the commit pinned in engine/UPSTREAM
and applies the patches with `git am`. On Linux, --weights nvfp4 instead clones the TensorFold fork
https://github.com/plotarmordev/TensorFold at the commit pinned in engine/nvfp4/UPSTREAM, also Apache-2.0,
and applies the ordered patches in engine/nvfp4/patches/ after checking their SHA256SUMS manifest. On Darwin,
--weights nvfp4 uses upstream TensorFold at engine/nvfp4/macos/UPSTREAM and applies the ordered patches in
engine/nvfp4/macos/patches/.

The patches modify TensorFold files. They add opt-in serving features and Drama 3 fixes: new files under
zig/src/server/, zig/src/core/, zig/src/native/, zig/kernels/metal/, zig/tests/, docs/ and tools/zig/,
and changes to existing TensorFold files in zig/build/, zig/src/core/, zig/src/families/drama3/,
zig/src/native/ and zig/src/server/, plus README.md and
CHANGELOG.md. Each patch's commit message and diff state what it changes. The patches keep TensorFold's existing
file headers and notices unchanged.

TensorFold's own NOTICE file reads:

    TensorFold
    Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors
    https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold

    TensorFold is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE) from 0.6.0.
    Releases up to 0.5.0 were MIT-licensed, and code written before 0.6.0 keeps its
    MIT notice in LICENSES/MIT.txt. Third-party code and its licenses are listed in
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

TensorFold's LICENSES/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are in the checkout that scripts/build-engine.sh creates.

SGLang-Omni
-----------
The recipe's sglang-omni backend and qualification tools run the SGLang-Omni Drama 3 reference implementation
(https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang-omni, sglang_omni/models/fishaudio_drama3, revision ab095ef9), whose
files carry SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0. They import it at run time; this repository does not include its
source files.

Fish Audio
----------
Built with Fish Audio.

This repository contains no Fish Audio model weights and no codec checkpoint. Users download the Drama 3 weights
and codec checkpoint separately from Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/fishaudio/drama-3), or the NVFP4 pruned
derivative (https://huggingface.co/plotarmordev/drama-3-NVFP4-Pruned) that recipe/pilot.py downloads. Those
files are licensed under the Fish Audio Community License, Version 1.0
